  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: 3rd person -s and questions with does (Does he/she ...?)",
      "title_form": "Presente simple: la -s de la tercera persona y preguntas con does",
      "title_target": "Present Simple: 3rd Person -s and Questions with Does",
      "description_md_form": "En inglés, cuando hablamos de **él** (he) o **ella** (she), el verbo cambia: le añadimos una **-s** al final. Por ejemplo: *He **sits** in the office.* (Él se sienta en la oficina).\n\nPara hacer **preguntas** sobre otra persona, usamos **does** al principio y el verbo vuelve a su forma base (sin -s):\n\n- *Does she **work** in the morning?* (¿Ella trabaja por la mañana?)\n- *Does he **sleep** after lunch?* (¿Él duerme después del almuerzo?)\n\n**Recuerda**: con *does*, el verbo no lleva -s. La -s ya está en el *does*.",
      "description_md_target": "In English, when we talk about **he** or **she**, the verb changes: we add an **-s** at the end. For example: *He **sits** in the office.*\n\nTo make **questions** about another person, we use **does** at the beginning and the verb goes back to its base form (without -s):\n\n- *Does she **work** in the morning?*\n- *Does he **sleep** after lunch?*\n\n**Remember**: with *does*, the verb does not take -s. The -s is already in the *does*.",
      "grammar_structure": "He/She + verb + -s | Does + he/she + verb (base form)?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_3rd_person",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Pregunta"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "I sit",
            "Do I sit?"
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "You sit",
            "Do you sit?"
          ],
          [
            "He/She",
            "He/She sits",
            "Does he/she sit?"
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "We sit",
            "Do we sit?"
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "They sit",
            "Do they sit?"
          ]
        ]
      },
